WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.780
How can one secreted signal tell embryonic cells what to become?

2
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.140
And why does it work by switching off a brake?

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.800
Most pathways you know add an active signal.

4
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.780
Hedgehog instead removes a brake.

5
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.220
Start across this row of developing cells.

6
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.920
The source on the left releases Hedgehog, which spreads outward and fades with

7
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.340
distance. Near cells see a high dose for longer, while distant cells see less.

8
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.380
Each cell converts that reading into a distinct fate.

9
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.560
Because concentration and duration steer cell identity, Hedgehog is a morphogen.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.720
Now zoom into the membrane of one receiving cell.

11
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.780
Two membrane proteins run the switch: Patched and Smoothened.

12
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.200
Without Hedgehog, Patched stays active and holds Smoothened off.

13
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.900
Notice that Patched never touches Smoothened.

14
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.660
A single Patched molecule can keep many Smoothened molecules quiet from a distance.

15
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.440
How can a brake work without grabbing its target?

16
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.860
Patched resembles a membrane transporter.

17
00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.860
In the leading model, Smoothened needs a sterol, likely cholesterol, to turn on.

18
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.380
Active Patched keeps that sterol out of reach.

19
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.560
What Patched actually moves, and what powers it, remain open questions.

20
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.090
Now Hedgehog arrives and binds Patched.

21
00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:35.910
Hedgehog carries lipid tails, and one plugs into Patched, switching the brake off.

22
00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.670
In the model, accessible sterol now reaches Smoothened, which lights up and turns

23
00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.270
on. Hedgehog never pressed an accelerator.

24
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:50.830
It switched off an off-switch, which is why the pathway is a double negative.

25
00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.293
What does Smoothened control inside the cell?

26
00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:57.793
Follow the transcription factor called Gli.

27
00:01:58.813 --> 00:02:03.653
While Smoothened is off, kinases add phosphates to Gli, marking it for the

28
00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:08.533
proteasome. The proteasome shreds only its back activating half.

29
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:15.093
The front DNA-binding piece survives and silences target genes as a repressor.

30
00:02:16.217 --> 00:02:17.717
Now pause and predict.

31
00:02:19.137 --> 00:02:22.417
Hedgehog arrives, Patched switches off, and Smoothened turns on.

32
00:02:23.637 --> 00:02:28.397
Does the cell glue cut repressors back together, or spare newly made Gli from being

33
00:02:28.397 --> 00:02:29.397
cut?

34
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:36.937
It spares newly made Gli from cutting.

35
00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:41.077
Once Smoothened turns on, kinase marking stops.

36
00:02:42.357 --> 00:02:44.857
Cut repressors are never glued back together.

37
00:02:46.237 --> 00:02:51.617
Instead, freshly made Gli avoids the proteasome, keeps its activating half intact,

38
00:02:52.057 --> 00:02:53.717
and moves into the nucleus whole.

39
00:02:55.057 --> 00:02:57.457
There, full-length Gli switches target genes on.

40
00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.527
Compare both states side by side.

41
00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:06.207
Without Hedgehog, Patched stays active, Smoothened stays off, and trimmed Gli

42
00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:12.487
silences genes. With Hedgehog, Patched turns off, Smoothened turns on, and intact

43
00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:13.627
Gli activates them.

44
00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:19.367
In short, Hedgehog switches off Patched, letting Smoothened keep Gli whole and

45
00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:19.747
active.
